  "query_preview": "/Sunday through Thursday/...\nHeat will stick around throughout the long-term period as a \nresult of a building high pressure aloft over the Four Corners \nregion. Valley temperatures will be in the mid to upper-90s \nthroughout the week next week (5-10 degrees above normal). A low\noff of the Alaskan Panhandle will keep our area under southwest\nflow aloft keeping the hottest temperatures to our south. A \npush of monsoonal moisture will give way to risk of \nthunderstorms beginning Monday through Wednesday. A shortwave \nMonday will also help enhance thunderstorm development Monday \nafternoon, details should become better resolved in the \nforecasts to come.",
